A||||10||FIEROGOD||FREINDS OR NOT||||1||
Z||000000||FIEROGOD||02-20-2001||01:40 AM|||| This is not a complaint it is a thought. I have been working with cars since i was 9 or 10. I have worked at three different car dealerships. And i have liked Fieros since they came out. I am 27and work with my dad, he has a car lot i have a repair shop.It seems that most if not all the people i hang with drive fieros. Now i don't mind this but i have to ask myself why they come around. A few of the people have become freinds. Along with that freindship comes cheaper rates for fixing their cars and sometimes no charge at all. I don't charge freinds as a rule. It seems that when they need help and i don't jump to help them they think i am an *******  or i don't respect them as a person. Or that i just don't give a **** . Not always but sometimes. I need to make a living. I sometimes tell them that i can help them on this day at this time but i don't because i know it won't get done in time or because i just don't want to do it. so i guess what i am asking are these people freinds or are they just people who get disscounts on their work? Are they right or am i wrong?<P>Expectations are the dissapointments of life. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||frontal lobe||02-20-2001||02:10 AM||||If the only time they come around now is when they need something, they aren't friends, they are leeches.  If they come around a lot anyway, and occasionally need something, they are probably really friends, but need to quit taking advantage of you.  You have a talent that you can turn into money.  If you take that time and talent to do something for them, you are really giving them money in essence.  That is unfair to you, and not being a good friend by them.<P>It's being a friend enough if you give them some sort of REASONABLE discount if you choose to, but it should never be their expectation.  In fact, if they are a good friend TO you, they will at least try to pay you the usual rate.||||reg||1
Z||000002||hugh||02-20-2001||07:25 AM||||You could post a sign somewhere in your shop in large letters THIS IS HOW I MAKE MY LIVING,ADVICE IS FREE,LABOR IS NOT.Or something to that effect.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||02-20-2001||07:49 AM||||Doctors and lawyers do not hesitate to draw the line regarding that.  I think you should too.  You're no less a professional than they are.  <P>Do those people have something free to offer you?  If so, there's no reason not to barter.  But don't let it become a one-way street.<P>This is all very easy for me to say, because I'm not in such a position as you, but you gotta have your principles.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000004||GT Bastard||02-20-2001||07:54 AM||||Ahhhhh... The best thing to do would be to tell the person from the beginning that you'd rather not get involved.  Don't set the expectation that you will help if really don't want to.  Your friends won't think any less of you if you don't want help them, but the very worst thing you can do is to tell them will and then back out or put it off indefinitely after you've already comitted yourself to it.  It shows a major lack of respect to them.  Exactly the type that your referring to.  In fact, it's probably a lot like being stabbed in the back by someone you trusted.  I know, because I was involved in a similar situation before.  Good luck!<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtbastard.gif">   <P>In my dreams I'm dying all the time...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||02-20-2001||10:08 AM||||I do a lot of work on friends cars. If I do the work I charge them. (with a "friend" discount of course) If they want to do the work I'll assist them (without charge) but they will do the actual work. Usually it is people who know how to work on their cars they just want help to do the work quickly.<BR>Like on a brake job one takes one side the other works on the opposite side. Gets done in half the time.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tigger||02-20-2001||10:32 AM||||I've heard several times on the board that if the friend brings over some beer and a pizza, that would be fine.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000007||onfire||02-20-2001||01:33 PM||||My uncle had a painting party for his house, He bought beer and a pizza for everyone. And the house was painted in a day.<P>P.S. I work for beer and pizza.||||reg||1
Z||000008||FIEROGOD||02-22-2001||12:03 AM||||Thanks.<P> Friends is a term used loosely by those who don't have true friends.||||reg||1
Z||000009||GT Bastard||02-22-2001||08:46 AM||||It's clear to me why you don't have "true" friends.  When I make a promise to a friend I keep it.  Especially if this friend has offered his assistance on numerous occasions without asking or expecting anything in return. ESPECIALLY when this friend has taken almost every oppurtunity to back you up when others shot you down behind you back. <P>PS- The Gold GT will be out of your lot soon. I already picked up the gaskets, oil, etc.. I'll be picking up the engine as soon as I can.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||2M4 Dale||02-22-2001||11:58 AM||||I own and opperate a small firearms shop. I sell and repair guns and accessories. It was simply amazing how many new "friends" I made when I opened my business...lol. I have, over the years, got it figured out that friends or not I am doing this to make money. An occational "good deal" for someone who helps me out somehow is fine.......other than that you gotta make a living. I don't make a living selling guns, it's just a side business but it's how I support my firearms hobby. Also, I sell Fiero parts (and other cars and parts too) here and elsewhere on the net.....I don't try to rob anybody.....I am using that cash profit to build myself a working garage/barn where I can support my Fiero sickness...lol. So "friends" or not I have to use my time to make money.......I know it sucks but thats what makes the world go round !||||reg||1
